=== Installation via Extreme Flash ===
Simply follow the documentation over at https://github.com/grische/extremeflash.

=== Installation via Serial/TFTP ===
Based on the [[commit>?p=openwrt/openwrt.git;a=commit;h=16b01fb1b9c99513c318109bef96a1a3545c57a0|initial commit description]].

  - Grab the OpenWrt initramfs, rename it to 01C8A8C0.img. Place it in \\  the root directory of a TFTP server and serve it at ''192.168.200.200/24''.
  - Connect to the serial port and boot the AP. Stop autoboot in U-Boot \\ by pressing Enter when prompted. Credentials are identical to the one in the APs interface.\\ By default it is ''admin'' / ''new2day''. If those credentials do not work, you can reset the device (including the U-Boot credentials) by holding the reset button for more than 10 seconds until the device resets.
  - Set the bootcmd so the AP can boot OpenWrt by executing<code>
$ setenv boot_openwrt "setenv bootargs; cp.b 0xee000000 0x1000000 0x1000000; bootm 0x1000000"
$ setenv bootcmd "run boot_openwrt"
$ saveenv
</code>\\ If you plan on going back to the vendor firmware - the bootcmd for it is stored in the ''boot_flash'' variable.
  - Load the initramfs image to RAM and boot by executing<code>
$ tftpboot 0x1000000 192.168.200.200:01C8A8C0.img; bootm
</code>
  - Make a backup of the "firmware" partition if you ever wish to go back to the vendor firmware.
  - Upload the OpenWrt sysupgrade image via SCP to the devices /tmp folder.
  - Flash OpenWrt using ''sysupgrade''.<code>
$ sysupgrade -n /tmp/openwrt-sysupgrade.bin
</code>

